[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115493,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Low-grade myofibroblastic sarcoma is a rarely metastasizing mesenchymal neoplasm, often having fibromatosis-like features, which tends to arise in the head and neck region.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-29T15:42:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115494,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8825/3 Low-grade myofibroblastic sarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-29T15:42:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115495,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B53.Y &amp; XH2668 Other specified fibroblastic or myofibroblastic tumour, primary site &amp; Low-grade myofibroblastic sarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-29T15:42:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115496,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> myofibrosarcoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-29T15:42:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115497,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-29T15:42:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115498,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The most common site is the tongue, followed by the larynx and gingiva {33302922}. Rarely these tumours arise in the nasal cavity and paranasal sinuses. They are mostly deeply seated; however, an origin in subcutaneous and submucosal sites does not exclude the diagnosis. Origin in the bone, notably the gnathic bones, can occur {31950474; 33302922; 9777985; 15173943; 24132324}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-29T15:42:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115499,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present with a slowly growing, painless mass. The average tumour size is 40&nbsp;mm {9777985; 33302922}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-29T15:42:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115500,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients can be affected at any age (median: 42&nbsp;years) {33302922; 9777985; 15173943}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-29T15:42:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115501,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-29T15:42:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115502,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Complex genetic aberrations have been identified, but the pathogenesis is unknown {10362810; 31950474}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-29T15:42:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115503,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are poorly marginated, grey-white, and firm, with a fibrous cut surface {9777985}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-29T15:42:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115504,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "<p>The pattern is that of a cellular, fibromatosis-like or fibrosarcoma-like lesion composed of fascicles or broad sheets of cells, with or without focal herringbone or storiform arrangement. Checkerboard-like infiltration of the adjacent skeletal muscle is a key diagnostic feature. The atypical myofibroblastic cells have enlarged, tapered, hyperchromatic nuclei and a scant or moderate amount of cytoplasm. Mitotic figures are variably present. The background can be collagenous or myxoid. Transformation into high-grade sarcoma has been reported {9777985; 24132324; 15173943}. There is a myofibroblastic immunophenotype showing variable expression of SMA, desmin, calponin, and CD34. H-caldesmon is reported to be focally expressed in a few cases. Expression of &beta;-catenin does not rule out this tumour type {9777985; 15173943; 31950474; 17711447}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-17T13:38:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115505,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-29T15:42:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115506,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant {31950474}</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-29T15:42:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115507,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> diffusely infiltrative growth, often between skeletal muscle fibres; cellular fascicles of spindle cells with pale eosinophilic cytoplasm; at least focally moderate nuclear atypia; variable expression of SMA and/or desmin.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-29T15:42:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115508,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-29T15:42:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115509,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Local recurrences are common, but metastatic spread to lung, soft tissue, and bone, often after a long interval, occurs rarely {9777985}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-29T15:42:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]